Date: 4 Nov 93 21:22:00 +1900
From: USR1593A@cbos.uc.edu
Subject: Stone Age

I feel like I'm in the Stone Age.  Imagine what it felt
like for Stone Age men and women when they acquired new
time saving devices at the dawn of technology.
With the wheel, axe, and plow they may have marveled at
how advanced they were over what had come before, and
rejoiced on how lucky it was that they were born into that
age. But, my GOD, they were IN the STONE AGE!!! So, true
for every age in history, and so, true for today.  We marvel
at our advances today and feel lucky; I, on the other hand,
feel disappointed that our sciences are so primitive and
long for an age when all our technological dreams of
development, knowledge, and exploration are old news.
Truly, this IS the STONE AGE! Bruce Zimov usr1593a@cbos.uc.edu

